{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1000,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is most effective for helping people\nlearn: punishment or reward?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5340,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, consider the case of Israeli fighter\npilot training, because instructors there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9470,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "found that negative feedback was far superior\nto positive feedback."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13130,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If a cadet performed a particularly poor maneuver\nthey would reprimand him."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17780,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But they noticed that on follow up attempts,\nhis performance invariably improved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21720,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In contrast, if they praised a cadet for executing\na skillful maneuver, his performance on subsequent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26660,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "attempts typically declined."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28720,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So naturally they concluded that positive\nfeedback is ineffective or even detrimental"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33190,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whereas negative feedback is what works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35640,
    "dDurationMs": 4790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem is this seems to contradict a\nbody of research that shows positive feedback"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40430,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is actually more effective than negative feedback."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43350,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, in studies involving teachers\nit was found that if a teacher increase the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47380,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ratio of positive feedback to negative feedback,\nthat actually increases the percentage of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52280,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "times students spend on task."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54760,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In another study rugby players were given\na video feedback session following a game,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59860,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "except half of them were shown their highlights\nand they were praised for what they had done"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63670,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the other half were shown their biggest\nblunders, their mistakes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67290,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they were scolded for doing things incorrectly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70350,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now a week later at the next game, it was\nthe players who had received the positive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74340,
    "dDurationMs": 1312,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reinforcement who performed the best."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75652,
    "dDurationMs": 4068,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, in fact, the difference was not just\npsychological."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79720,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Blood tests revealed that the players who\nreceived positive feedback actually had higher"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83590,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "levels of testosterone than players who had\nreceived the negative feedback."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88170,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think that is quite remarkable that even\na week post feedback you could still see a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92890,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physiological difference between the two types\nof feedback."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96740,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97740,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well so why didn't this work for the Israeli\nfighter pilots?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101520,
    "dDurationMs": 4099,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, maybe there are cultural differences\nand in some cultures negative feedback works"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105619,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "better."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106619,
    "dDurationMs": 2151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or maybe it is task dependent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108770,
    "dDurationMs": 4489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps some skills like learning to fly a\nfighter jet require more negative feedback."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113259,
    "dDurationMs": 4970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or maybe the feedback had nothing to do with\nthe performance of the fighter pilots at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118229,
    "dDurationMs": 4850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe they would have performed in the same\nway regardless of the feedback they received."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123079,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Go with me on this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124939,
    "dDurationMs": 5501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine you have 100 students taking a test\nwhich consists of 100 true or false questions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130440,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on a subject they know nothing about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132690,
    "dDurationMs": 4879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now assuming they all answer randomly, we\nknow that the resulting distribution of scores"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137569,
    "dDurationMs": 2551,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will have an average of around 50."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140120,
    "dDurationMs": 4699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But just by chance, some students will have\nscored significantly better or worse than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144819,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the average."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145819,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Oh, man."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146819,
    "dDurationMs": 4901,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e If you select the top 10 students whose\nscores were all above 50 and gave them a second"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151720,
    "dDurationMs": 4670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very similar test, you would find that the\naverage of their scores would drop back to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156390,
    "dDurationMs": 1420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around 50."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157810,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, if you selected the bottom 10 students,\ntheir score on a subsequent test would rise"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163430,
    "dDurationMs": 1190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to 50."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164620,
    "dDurationMs": 2410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is just regression to the mean."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167030,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Regression to the mean is the reason why if\nyou have a really good round of golf today,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170650,
    "dDurationMs": 3230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your round tomorrow will not be as good."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173880,
    "dDurationMs": 1550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175430,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is because random chance plays a role\nin virtually everything that we do."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179270,
    "dDurationMs": 5579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the outcomes of events are influenced by\nboth our skill and a little bit of luck."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184849,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you have especially good luck on one\nday, chances are your level of luck will not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189099,
    "dDurationMs": 1941,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be as good the next day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191040,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that sounds a little bit like the gamblers\nfallacy, which states that past events influence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197080,
    "dDurationMs": 1269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "future probabilities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198349,
    "dDurationMs": 3731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, if you flip a coin and it comes\nup tails a couple of times, the gamblers fallacy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202080,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is to expect the probability of heads to increase\nfor the next flip."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206190,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In reality it doesn’t."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207190,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is still 50-50."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208190,
    "dDurationMs": 5549,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The idea wit the gamblers fallacy is that\nprobabilities change so that overall things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213739,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over out in the long run."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215209,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the idea."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216769,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With regression to the mean, it is not that\nthings are evening out, it is just that extreme"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220459,
    "dDurationMs": 5030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "events are becoming diluted by the average\nevents which happen much more commonly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225489,
    "dDurationMs": 3351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now with these students they were completely\nguessing on every question."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228840,
    "dDurationMs": 2710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But even when you know something about the\nsubject, there is still going to be there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231550,
    "dDurationMs": 1439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that element of chance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232989,
    "dDurationMs": 4411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so regression to the mean always occurs,\njust to a lesser extent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237400,
    "dDurationMs": 2510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is really important to consider in research."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239910,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine you are trialing a new drug to help\nprevent heart disease."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243190,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So from a sample of patients you select those\nin the bottom 10 percent of heart health indicators,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248130,
    "dDurationMs": 3130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people with high blood pressure, high cholesterol,\nthat sort of thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251260,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now after a month of being on a drug, you\ntest them again to find that their scores"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254640,
    "dDurationMs": 1010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have improved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255650,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, great, the drug is working, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258810,
    "dDurationMs": 1130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, maybe not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259940,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, the trouble is that although blood pressure\nand cholesterol are more stable than, say,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263960,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your score on a random true or false test,\nthere is still some inherent variability caused"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268620,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by, say, your level of stress on the day or\nyour recent diet or even the uncertainties"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273240,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "introduced by the measuring apparatus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275150,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the people who ended up in the bottom 10\npercent on the first test, likely had these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279180,
    "dDurationMs": 1630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "factors all count against them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280810,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were particularly unlucky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282330,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you should not expect them to be as unlucky\nwhen you test them a second time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286830,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So their scores should improve just based\non random chance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290680,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is why it is so important that clinical\ntrials use control groups drawn from exactly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294960,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same population so that you can see whether\nthe drug improves scores more than random"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300020,
    "dDurationMs": 1970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chance alone would."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301990,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or what about the assessing the impact of\nspeed cameras?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304990,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When they are first installed, they are normally\nput in locations that have had a high volume"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308560,
    "dDurationMs": 2290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of accidents in the previous year or two."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310850,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Makes sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311850,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now those accidents are likely due, at least\nin part, to bad road design, but also due,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316270,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at least in part, to bad luck."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318730,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so you shouldn’t be surprised that after\na speed camera is installed the number of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323590,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "accidents goes down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325730,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would go down anyway simply due to regression\nto the mean."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329910,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile somewhere else that previously had\na small number of accidents will likely have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334540,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335540,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the overall accident rate may not change\nand yet we will feel as though our investment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340350,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in road safety has paid off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343370,
    "dDurationMs": 4109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But perhaps what is most troubling about regression\nto the mean is how it influences our perception"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347479,
    "dDurationMs": 1381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of feedback."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348860,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, with the fighter pilots, after\nthey execute a maneuver particularly poorly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353430,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chances are the next attempt is going to be\nbetter, regardless of the feedback they receive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358990,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, after an especially successful\ndisplay, chances are the next attempt is not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364030,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "going to be as good."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365780,
    "dDurationMs": 3490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that has nothing to do with the feedback\nand everything to do with the statistical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369270,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nature of our universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371130,
    "dDurationMs": 5290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we are hard wired to see patterns and\ncausality everywhere, which is why the instructors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376420,
    "dDurationMs": 5370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "felt that positive feedback was detrimental\nand negative feedback is what works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381790,
    "dDurationMs": 3999,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is really unfortunate, because that\nis the exact opposite of what well controlled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385789,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "psychological studies show."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388169,
    "dDurationMs": 3961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, I think it is really unfortunate\nthat if you give negative feedback, chances"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392130,
    "dDurationMs": 1810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are you will be rewarded."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393940,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They will do better."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395500,
    "dDurationMs": 3530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you give positive feedback, chances\nare you will be disappointed, because it is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399030,
    "dDurationMs": 3919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "difficult to maintain that level of luck."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402949,
    "dDurationMs": 2531,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that is the way our world is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405480,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So think about that next time before you tell\nsomeone off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409380,
    "dDurationMs": 5450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you stay positive, it may just work out\nfor the best in the long run."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414830,
    "dDurationMs": 6839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video was inspired by the book Thinking\nFast and Slow by Nobel prize winning economist"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421669,
    "dDurationMs": 1541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Daniel Kahneman."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423210,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that was the first time I heard of the\nIsraeli fighter pilot training and really"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427250,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "started thinking about regression to the mean."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429710,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was pretty awesome and I downloaded this\nbook from Audible, so I was listening to it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433080,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on my travels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434080,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
